@startuml
title UC-01 - Create / Configure Application (Main Flow)

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Developer
boundary "Web UI" as UI
control "Application API / Controller" as API
control "Application Service" as Service
control "Application Definition Validator" as Validator
entity "Application Repository" as AppRepo
control "Application Specification Generator" as SpecGenerator
entity "Specification Repository /\nConfig Repo Service" as SpecRepo

Developer -> UI: Select Create Application\nor open an existing application

alt Create a new application
    UI -> API: createApplication(name, description)
    API -> Service: createApplication(name, description)
    Service --> API: Application draft
    API --> UI: Display application editor
else Update an existing application
    UI -> API: updateApplication(applicationId)
    API -> Service: updateApplication(applicationId)
    Service -> AppRepo: findLatestVersion(applicationId)
    AppRepo --> Service: Latest Application Definition version\n(components with stable IDs)
    Service --> API: Editable Application Definition draft\nbased on the latest version
    API --> UI: Display application editor
end

Developer -> UI: Add resource requirements
UI -> API: addResourceRequirement(applicationId, resources)
API -> Service: addResourceRequirement(applicationId, resources)

Developer -> UI: Add workloads\n(type, image repository, port)
UI -> API: addWorkload(applicationId, workloads)
API -> Service: addWorkload(applicationId, workloads)

Developer -> UI: Define environment variables and secrets\nfor each workload
UI -> API: defineConfigurationRequirement(applicationId, requirements)
API -> Service: defineConfigurationRequirement(applicationId, requirements)

Developer -> UI: Define dependencies
UI -> API: defineDependency(applicationId, dependencies)
API -> Service: defineDependency(applicationId, dependencies)

Service --> API: Updated Application Definition draft
API --> UI: Display topology and configuration summary
UI --> Developer: Show application overview

Developer -> UI: Select Save Application
UI -> API: saveApplicationDefinition(applicationDefinition)
API -> Service: saveApplicationDefinition(applicationDefinition)
Service -> Validator: validateApplicationDefinition(applicationDefinition)
Validator --> Service: Validation successful
Service -> AppRepo: saveNewVersion(applicationDefinition)
AppRepo --> Service: New Application Definition version saved
note right of AppRepo
  Every save creates a new immutable version.
  Existing versions are never updated or deleted.
  Workloads, resources, environment variable definitions
  and secret definitions keep stable IDs across versions:
  renaming keeps the ID; removing a component only means
  the new version no longer contains it.
  No environment changes until the version is deployed (UC-03).
end note
Service -> SpecGenerator: generateApplicationSpecification(applicationDefinitionVersion)
SpecGenerator --> Service: Application specification (for example, score.yaml)
Service -> SpecRepo: save(applicationSpecification)
SpecRepo --> Service: Specification saved
Service --> API: Application version saved
API --> UI: Show save confirmation
UI --> Developer: New Application Definition version and specification saved

@enduml
